        {
          "text": "FA Jo-chên 法若真 (T. 漢儒, H. 黃石, 黃山), 1613–1696, scholar, official, and landscape painter, was a native of Kiaochow, Shantung. His father, Fa Huan 法寰 (T. 開三, chü-jên of 1627, d. 1653), served as magistrate of three districts in Chihli and Kiangsu, as first-class sub-prefect of Huai-ch'ing-fu, Honan, and when the Ming dynasty fell retired to his home.",
